    "short_label": {
      "en": "$tin_wkintc_amt"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "Maximum annual amount of a tax credit for low earned income introduced in Spain's IRPF since 2025, the 'Deduccion por obtencion de rendimientos del trabajo' - a deduction from the general tax base for taxpayers with modest wage income. Used as the Comp_perTU parameter of BenCalc in tinit_es and tinjt_es. The Country Report describes this measure as a deduction of up to 340 euro/year for annual work income at or below its first limit ($tin_wkintc_lim1), tapering to zero by the second limit ($tin_wkintc_lim2) at a 20% withdrawal rate; the modelled maximum amount (590.89 euro) is higher than the Country Report's stated 340 euro figure, likely reflecting a later legislative revision of the measure not captured in the report's narrative text."
    },
